SetupCache: retain immutable LUT ownership across LRU changes.

Co-created with GPT (OpenAI), 2026-11-08.
The old pointer named an element in a rotating/reallocating vector. A second
session could rotate, reallocate or evict it while a pipeline uploaded/copied
the LUT after releasing the cache mutex. Give each caller shared immutable
ownership through that upload/copy. Numerical builders, keys and values do
not change. Retained payloads are released when their last reader finishes.

diff --git a/engine/src/core/setup_cache.hpp b/engine/src/core/setup_cache.hpp
--- a/engine/src/core/setup_cache.hpp
+++ b/engine/src/core/setup_cache.hpp
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
 #pragma once
+#include <memory>
 #include <mutex>
 #include <string>
 #include <unordered_map>
 #include <vector>

@@ -55,12 +56,12 @@ public:
-    // The spectral upsampling LUT. `out` points into the cache and stays
-    // valid until this cache is destroyed.
+    // The spectral upsampling LUT. Each reader owns the immutable payload,
+    // including across LRU rotations/eviction and cache destruction.
     bool tc_lut(const Colour& colour, const Blob& blob, const Profile& film,
                 const SettingsParams& settings, const GamutCompressSpec& compress,
-                const Vec& sensitivity, const Vec*& out, size_t& side, std::string& error);
+                const Vec& sensitivity, std::shared_ptr<const Vec>& out, size_t& side, std::string& error);

     // For `capabilities`, and for anyone wondering whether a slider was slow
     // because of a miss.
     struct Stats { size_t cam16_entries = 0, lut_entries = 0, hits = 0, misses = 0; };
     Stats stats() const;

 private:
@@ -73,6 +74,6 @@ private:
     struct LutEntry {
         std::string key;
-        Vec lut;
+        std::shared_ptr<const Vec> lut;
         size_t side = 0;
     };

